{"id":"398f1e34941ebd2bbcde6a71c7683bebba57d174","axis":"silent","repo":"oven-sh/bun","sha":"398f1e34941ebd2bbcde6a71c7683bebba57d174","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/pm/bunx.mdx","lines":["@@ -46,6 +46,8 @@ bunx my-cli"," "," As with `npx`, `bunx` checks for a locally installed package first, then falls back to auto-installing it from `npm`. With a version (`bunx my-cli@2`), it does not use the local package. `bunx` stores installed packages in Bun's [global cache](/pm/global-cache) for future use."," ","+On macOS and Linux, if the project has the package but the file of its executable is missing or has no execute permission, `bunx my-cli` exits with an error that names the file. It does not download another copy.","+"," `bunx my-cli` asks the registry for newer versions of the package and of its dependencies once a day. If the registry cannot be reached or answers with a 5xx, 429 or 408 status, it warns and runs the version it has. `bunx my-cli@latest` asks on every run."," "," ## Arguments and flags"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/pm/cli/update.mdx","lines":["@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@ Updated packages appear in the install summary as `↑ name old → new`, with `"," - Bun does not add a version that another one covers. Two dependencies declaring `foo@^1` and `foo@*` share one `1.x` copy, as on `bun install`. Versions already in `bun.lock` and your own `package.json` entries are never moved to save a copy."," - Versions in `patchedDependencies` stay put as long as their range allows. Bun reports them as `kept name@version (patched, v1.2.3 available)`. `--latest` and [`bun audit fix`](/pm/cli/audit#bun-audit-fix) do move them; re-create the patch with [`bun patch`](/pm/cli/patch) afterwards."," - If a registry request for a transitive package fails, that package keeps its locked version and Bun prints a warning. A failed request for a direct dependency is an error.","+- An optional dependency on a git repository, a GitHub repository, or a tarball keeps its locked package when Bun cannot fetch that source. Bun prints `warn: name@version was not checked for updates`. This does not apply to a dependency that an [`overrides`](/pm/overrides) rule or a catalog sets. If you pass the `package.json` key of the dependency, or if `--prod` or `--depth 0` selects it, `bun update` exits with code 1 and writes nothing."," "," ## `--interactive`"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/pm/overrides.mdx","lines":["@@ -103,6 +103,8 @@ A value can be any dependency specifier, not only a version range. `npm:` swaps"," }"," ```"," ","+Bun reads a value like the specifier of a dependency that has the name in the rule's key. A `catalog:` rule reads the catalog entry of that name, and `workspace:*` links the workspace of that name. For a key that spells an `npm:` alias, the name is the alias: `\"my-foo@npm:foo@^1\": \"catalog:\"` reads the `my-foo` entry, and not the `foo` entry.","+"," Bun warns about a `catalog:` rule whose package is not in the catalog. A dependency that the rule applies to then fails to resolve."," "," A value of `\"$name\"` reuses the range you declared for `name` in your own dependencies, so `\"bar\": \"$foo\"` pins `bar` to whatever range you declared for `foo`.","@@ -165,7 +167,7 @@ Bun compares the selector with the range each dependent _declares_, not the reso"," Two more selectors match a dependency by how it is declared, like Yarn's `\"resolutions\"`:"," "," - `\"foo@catalog:\"` (or `\"foo@catalog:name\"`) applies to dependents that declare `foo` with that [catalog](/pm/catalogs).","-- `\"my-foo@npm:foo@^1\"` applies to an `npm:` alias named `my-foo` that points at `foo` with an overlapping range. No other rule overrides an alias.","+- `\"my-foo@npm:foo@^1\"` applies to an `npm:` alias named `my-foo` that points at `foo` with an overlapping range. No other rule overrides an alias that has a version range. An alias of a dist-tag, such as `\"my-foo\": \"npm:foo@latest\"`, takes the rules for `foo`."," "," ## Limitations"," "],"additions":3,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/bundler/bundle_v2.rs","lines":["@@ -6801,9 +6801,13 @@ pub mod bv2_impl {","                     }"," ","                     if import_record.path.text.starts_with(b\"bun:\") {","-                        let new_text: &'static [u8] = &import_record.path.text[b\"bun:\".len()..];","-                        import_record.path = bun_paths::fs::Path::init(new_text);","-                        import_record.path.namespace = b\"bun\";","+                        if let Some(builtin) =","+                            bun_resolve_builtins::HardcodedModule::Alias::bun_prefixed_builtin(","+                                import_record.path.text,","+                            )","+                        {","+                            import_record.path = bun_paths::fs::Path::init(builtin);","+                        }","                         import_record.source_index = Index::INVALID;","                         import_record","                             .flags"],"additions":7,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/bundler/linker.rs","lines":["@@ -406,10 +406,10 @@ impl Linker {","                             continue;","                         }"," ","-                        if strings::has_prefix_comptime(import_record.path.text, b\"bun:\") {","-                            import_record.path =","-                                PFs::Path::init(&import_record.path.text[b\"bun:\".len()..]);","-                            import_record.path.namespace = b\"bun\";","+                        if let Some(builtin) = bun_resolve_builtins::Alias::bun_prefixed_builtin(","+                            import_record.path.text,","+                        ) {","+                            import_record.path = PFs::Path::init(builtin);","                         }","                     }","                 }"],"additions":4,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/collections/zig_hash_map.rs","lines":["@@ -494,6 +494,17 @@ impl<K, V, C: HashContext<K>> HashMap<K, V, C> {","             .map(|(k, v)| crate::hash_map::KV { key: k, value: v })","     }"," ","+    /// std `retain`. Calls `keep` exactly once per entry.","+    pub fn retain(&mut self, mut keep: impl FnMut(&K, &mut V) -> bool) {","+        for idx in 0..self.slots.len() {","+            if let Some((key, value)) = &mut self.slots[idx]","+                && !keep(key, value)","+            {","+                let _ = self.remove_by_index(idx);","+            }","+        }","+    }","+","     /// std `entry` API. `VacantEntry::insert` does a second probe (re-runs","     /// `get_or_put_slot`); acceptable for the few callers that use it.","     pub fn entry(&mut self, key: K) -> MapEntry<'_, K, V, C> {","@@ -680,3 +691,45 @@ impl<'a, K, V, C: HashContext<K>> VacantEntry<'a, K, V, C> {","         &mut self.map.slots[idx].as_mut().unwrap().1","     }"," }","+","+#[cfg(test)]","+mod retain_tests {","+    use super::*;","+","+    /// `keep` is shown each entry once, and the entries it accepts are still found by key.","+    fn check(keys: &[u64], rejected: &[u64]) {","+        // The home slot is `key & 7`, so the keys choose the runs.","+        let mut map: HashMap<u64, u32, IdentityContext<u64>> = HashMap::new();","+        for &key in keys {","+            map.insert(key, 0);","+        }","+        assert_eq!(map.capacity(), 8);","+        map.retain(|key, shown| {","+            *shown += 1;","+            !rejected.contains(key)","+        });","+        let mut left: Vec<(u64, u32)> = map.iter().map(|(key, shown)| (*key, *shown)).collect();","+        left.sort_unstable();","+        let mut expected: Vec<(u64, u32)> = (keys.iter().filter(|key| !rejected.contains(key)))","+            .map(|&key| (key, 1))","+            .collect();","+        expected.sort_unstable();","+        assert_eq!(left, expected);","+        assert_eq!(map.len(), expected.len());","+        for (key, _) in expected {","+            assert_eq!(map.get(&key), Some(&1));","+        }","+    }","+","+    #[test]","+    fn retain_shows_each_entry_once() {","+        // 2 and 10 share home slot 2: 10 is in slot 3, behind the rejected entry.","+        check(&[2, 10, 3], &[2]);","+        check(&[2, 10, 3], &[2, 10]);","+        // The run wraps: 6 in slot 6, 14 in slot 7, 22 in slot 0.","+        check(&[6, 14, 22], &[6]);","+        check(&[6, 14, 22], &[14]);","+        check(&[6, 14, 22, 30, 7, 15], &[6, 30]);","+        check(&[2, 10, 3], &[]);","+    }","+}"],"additions":53,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/install/PackageInstaller.rs","lines":["@@ -2084,17 +2084,14 @@ impl<'a> PackageInstaller<'a> {","                             context,","                         )","                     }","-                    resolution::Tag::LocalTarball => {","-                        package_manager::enqueue_tarball_for_reading(","-                            self.manager_mut(),","-                            dependency_id,","-                            package_id,","-                            alias.slice(string_buf!()),","-                            resolution,","-                            context,","-                        );","-                        Ok(())","-                    }","+                    resolution::Tag::LocalTarball => package_manager::enqueue_tarball_for_reading(","+                        self.manager_mut(),","+                        dependency_id,","+                        package_id,","+                        alias.slice(string_buf!()),","+                        resolution,","+                        context,","+                    ),","                     resolution::Tag::RemoteTarball => {","                         package_manager::enqueue_tarball_for_download(","                             self.manager_mut(),"],"additions":8,"deletions":11,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/install/PackageManager/Pack